From: Neutron
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: present with premultiplied alpha into a window that enabled DWM blur-behind

A blt-model (DISCARD/SEQUENTIAL) swap chain presents into its window's own surface, and once the window has
called DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow, Windows' compositor blends that surface by its pixels' alpha. Qt makes its
translucent Direct3D windows this way (frameless, LWA_ALPHA 255, blur-behind with an empty region). The
presenter always asked Vulkan for VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_OPAQUE_BIT_KHR, so the transparent part of such a window
came out black: CapCut 9.7's menus are popups the size of the screen, and opening one blacked out the screen
around it.

Wine's dwmapi (Neutron patch 117) marks a blur-behind window __wine_dwm_alpha. When a blt-model swap chain's
window carries the mark at swap chain (re)creation and the surface supports it, the presenter now uses
VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_PRE_MULTIPLIED_BIT_KHR (logged "neutron-premultiplied"). Flip-model and composition swap
chains, and every unmarked window, are unchanged. The present shaders and the blitter already keep alpha.

Lab, CapCut 9.7 (NVIDIA, Wayland surface offers OPAQUE + PRE_MULTIPLIED): menu over the editor 3 of 3;
NEUTRON_DXVK_PREMULTIPLIED=0 on the same build, black 1 of 1. Kill switch NEUTRON_DXVK_PREMULTIPLIED=0.

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
index 472789e9..aecf5275 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
@@ -995,6 +995,8 @@ namespace dxvk {
     // test the Wine dcomp bridge mark. m_surfaceFactory is always a
     // DxgiSurfaceFactory (sole implementer of IDXGIVkSurfaceFactory).
     presenterDesc.window = static_cast<DxgiSurfaceFactory*>(m_surfaceFactory.ptr())->GetWindow();
+    presenterDesc.windowAlpha = m_desc.SwapEffect == DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_DISCARD
+                             || m_desc.SwapEffect == DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_SEQUENTIAL;
 
     m_presenter = new Presenter(m_device, m_frameLatencySignal, presenterDesc, [
       cAdapter  = m_device->adapter(),
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp
index b84c2918..a869bf83 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp
@@ -63,7 +63,8 @@ namespace dxvk {
     m_vki(device->instance()->vki()),
     m_vkd(device->vkd()),
     m_surfaceProc(std::move(proc)),
-    m_window(desc.window) {
+    m_window(desc.window),
+    m_windowAlpha(desc.windowAlpha) {
     // Only enable FSE if the user explicitly opts in. On Windows, FSE
     // is required to support VRR or HDR, but blocks alt-tabbing or
     // overlapping windows, which breaks a number of games.
@@ -899,6 +900,21 @@ namespace dxvk {
     swapInfo.imageSharingMode       = VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE;
     swapInfo.preTransform           = VK_SURFACE_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY_BIT_KHR;
     swapInfo.compositeAlpha         = VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_OPAQUE_BIT_KHR;
+
+    // neutron: a blt-model swap chain presents into its window's own surface, and once the window
+    // enabled DWM blur-behind, Windows' compositor blends that surface by its alpha. Qt's translucent
+    // Direct3D windows rely on it (CapCut's menus are full-window translucent popups drawn this way).
+    // Hand the alpha to the compositor when the surface can take it; OPAQUE otherwise, as before.
+    // Checked at every swap chain (re)creation.
+    bool premultiplied = m_windowAlpha && m_window
+      && GetPropW(reinterpret_cast<HWND>(m_window), L"__wine_dwm_alpha");
+
+    if (premultiplied
+     && (caps.surfaceCapabilities.supportedCompositeAlpha & VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_PRE_MULTIPLIED_BIT_KHR)
+     && env::getEnvVar("NEUTRON_DXVK_PREMULTIPLIED") != "0") {
+      swapInfo.compositeAlpha       = VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_PRE_MULTIPLIED_BIT_KHR;
+      Logger::info(str::format("neutron-premultiplied: window ", m_window, ", composite alpha PRE_MULTIPLIED"));
+    }
     swapInfo.presentMode            = m_presentMode;
     swapInfo.clipped                = VK_TRUE;
 
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.h b/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.h
index cb823770..4268e0c1 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.h
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.h
@@ -40,6 +40,10 @@ namespace dxvk {
     // only to test the Wine dcomp bridge mark (__wine_dcomp_blit). void*
     // keeps this header platform-agnostic; it is an HWND on Win32.
     void* window = nullptr;
+    // neutron: a blt-model swap chain. On Windows its presents land in the window's own surface,
+    // which DWM blends by its alpha once the window enabled blur-behind (Wine's dwmapi marks such
+    // a window __wine_dwm_alpha); present with premultiplied alpha then.
+    bool windowAlpha = false;
   };
 
   /**
@@ -284,6 +288,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
     // the stamp (m_boundedAcquire, set via INeutronBoundedAcquire) is the
     // primary scoping signal and the window mark only a fallback.
     void*                       m_window = nullptr;
+    bool                        m_windowAlpha = false;
 
     // neutron-bounded-acquire: sticky "this chain is readback-blitted" flag
     std::atomic<bool>           m_boundedAcquire = { false };
